{"name":"San Antonio Sage","hex":"#a69474","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"san","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-3 language code for Sanskrit."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An Ancient Greek letter representing /s/ (uppercase Ϻ, lowercase ϻ), originally used in some dialects instead of sigma."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/san"},{"term":"sage","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Wise.","Grave; serious; solemn."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A very wise person or spiritual teacher; someone of gravity and wisdom, especially, a teacher venerable for years, and of sound judgment and prudence; a grave or stoic philosopher."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sage"}],"entries":[{"title":"San Antonio","blocks":[{"text":"San Antonio is a city in the southern part of the U.S. state of Texas. It is the seventh-most populous city in the United States, the second-most populous city in Texas, and the second-most populous city in the Southern U.S., with a population of 1.43 million at the 2020 census. The Greater San Antonio metropolitan area, with an estimated 2.76 million residents, ranks as the third-largest metropolitan area in Texas and the 24th-largest in the nation. It is the county seat of Bexar County."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/San_Antonio_Botanical_Garden_Overlook_View.jpg/330px-San_Antonio_Botanical_Garden_Overlook_View.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/San_Antonio"},{"title":"Antonio","blocks":[{"text":"Antonio is a masculine given name of probably Etruscan origin deriving from the root name Antonius. It is a common name among Romance language–speaking populations as well as the Balkans and Lusophone Africa. It has been among the top 400 most popular male baby names in the United States since the late 19th century and has been among the top 200 since the mid 20th century."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antonio"},{"title":"Sage (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Sage is a grey-green resembling that of dried sage leaves. As a quaternary color, it is an equal mix of the tertiary colors citron and slate. The hex RGB color value of the adjacent sage swatch is BCB88A. For decades, some military flight jackets were made in sage green."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Sage_iPhone_17.jpg/330px-Sage_iPhone_17.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sage_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Downtown_San_Antonio_view_from_The_Tower_of_the_Americas.jpg/500px-Downtown_San_Antonio_view_from_The_Tower_of_the_Americas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Downtown_San_Antonio_view_from_The_Tower_of_the_Americas.jpg/1280px-Downtown_San_Antonio_view_from_The_Tower_of_the_Americas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Downtown_San_Antonio_view_from_The_Tower_of_the_Americas.jpg/500px-Downtown_San_Antonio_view_from_The_Tower_of_the_Americas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADowntown_San_Antonio_view_from_The_Tower_of_the_Americas.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/San_Antonio_Riverwalk_with_boat_tour_view.jpg/500px-San_Antonio_Riverwalk_with_boat_tour_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/San_Antonio_Riverwalk_with_boat_tour_view.jpg/500px-San_Antonio_Riverwalk_with_boat_tour_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=